menu "app_btn -- the panel buttons"

config APP_BTN_ENABLE
    bool "Read the panel's buttons"
    default y
    help
        Three of the Inky Impression's four tactile buttons (PLAN 3b). Harmless with
        nothing wired: an unconnected pin sits high on its pull-up, which is what an
        unpressed button reads as.

config APP_BTN_A_GPIO
    int "Button A"
    default 7
    help
        XIAO D5, Pi header 29.

config APP_BTN_B_GPIO
    int "Button B"
    default 21
    help
        XIAO D6, Pi header 31. Ordinary GPIO on this board only because the console is on
        USB Serial/JTAG rather than UART0 -- see sdkconfig.defaults.esp32c3.

config APP_BTN_C_GPIO
    int "Button C"
    default 20
    help
        XIAO D7, Pi header 36. As with D6, free only because UART0 is not the console.

config APP_BTN_DEBOUNCE_MS
    int "Debounce (ms)"
    default 40
    help
        A press must read low for this long before it counts. Polled rather than
        interrupt-driven: a button pressed by a finger is a slow event, the panel task is
        the only thing with deadlines, and a poll cannot storm the scheduler the way a
        bouncing edge on an ISR can.

config APP_BTN_LONG_PRESS_MS
    int "Long press (ms)"
    default 1500
    help
        Held at least this long reports as a long press. Used for the actions that should
        not happen by brushing against the panel.

endmenu
